# PORTAL-001 / F-05 — release signing, by example.
#
# COPY, DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE:
#     cp android/key.properties.example android/key.properties
#
# `android/key.properties` and every `*.jks` / `*.keystore` are gitignored.
# NEVER commit the real file, the keystore, or these passwords. Losing the
# keystore means the app can never be upgraded again — it is a permanent
# credential, so treat it like the JWT signing key: a secret store, with a
# backup somewhere the person who set it up is not the only one who can reach.
#
# In CI, write this file from secrets immediately before the build and delete
# it immediately after. Do not export the passwords as environment variables
# that a build log could echo.

# Path to the keystore, absolute or relative to android/app/ — NOT to this
# file. Gradle resolves it with `file()` inside the app module, so a keystore
# that sits beside this file at android/lacteva-release.jks must be written
# with the `../`:
#
#     storeFile=../lacteva-release.jks
#
# A bare `lacteva-release.jks` sends Gradle looking in android/app/ and the
# build fails with "Keystore file ... not found" (WO-67, the first release
# build this project ran). An absolute path avoids the question entirely.
storeFile=../lacteva-release.jks
storePassword=CHANGEME-keystore-password
keyAlias=lacteva-release
keyPassword=CHANGEME-key-password
